.env
# data/chunks.json and data/vocab.yaml ARE sent to the build context and
# COPYed into the image now — this repo has no other way to get the corpus
# onto a hosting platform. logs/ stays excluded: it's a local-dev-only
# junction (see .gitignore), write-only runtime state, never a build input.
logs/
# Unlike .gitignore, dockerignore patterns are NOT recursive by default —
# `__pycache__/` alone only matched the context root, not backend/backend/
# __pycache__/, and a stray one leaked into a real build (caught by actually
# running the image and looking, not by reading this file and assuming).
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.venv/
.git/
